  "nl_text": "The rschema_0247 database is designed to manage user information and academic records for a school system. The User table stores details about each user, including their username, password, registration time, role, and student ID, with a unique identifier for each user. The Class table contains information about the different classes offered, such as the class name, grade level, and major. The Sign-in table tracks when each user logs in, recording the IP address, sign-in status, and time, and links this information to the corresponding user. The Course table lists the various courses available, including their descriptions, names, and the teacher responsible, with a foreign key referencing the User table to establish the teacher's identity. The Control_Flag table records the start and end times for teacher control flags, linking this information to the teacher's User ID. The Grade table stores the grades for each student in each course, including the final, regular, and total grades, and links this information to the Course and User tables to establish the course and student identities.",
  "gold_question": "The system includes the following functionalities:\n1.Registration and Login Functionality\nNew User Registration: Teachers and students can register new accounts. The system must verify the uniqueness of student ID or teacher ID.\nUser Login: After registration, users can log in to the system. The system must authenticate the user’s identity to prevent impersonation.\nUser Information: Each user has a unique user ID, username, password, student number (or teacher ID), role, registration time, and last login time.\n2.Sign-in Functionality\nStudent Sign-in: Students can sign in online. The system uses IP address and time constraints to prevent impersonation and multiple sign-ins. The system records the current sign-in status.\nTeacher Control Sign-in: Teachers can start and stop sign-in through control flags, view sign-in details. The control flag includes flag ID, teacher ID, sign-in start time, and end time.\n3.Statistics Functionality\nStudent Attendance Statistics: The system records each sign-in event and uses the total sign-in count to calculate the student’s regular performance.\n4.Class and Course Management\nClass Information: Each student’s class includes class name, major, and grade.\nCourse Information: Each course includes course name and description.\nRelationships: Each class has multiple students, and each course is taught by a teacher.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0247.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0247\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `student_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `username` (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `class` (\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `class_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `grade_level` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `major` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`class_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sign_in` (\n  `sign_in_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `sign_in_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `sign_in_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sign_in_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sign_in_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `teacher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`teacher_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `control_flag` (\n  `control_flag_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `teacher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`control_flag_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `control_flag_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`teacher_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `grade` (\n  `grade_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `final_grade` float NOT NULL,\n  `regular_grade` float NOT NULL,\n  `total_grade` float NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`grade_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `grade_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `grade_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
